# SABOTAGE: the fail-honest "could not be read" state is DROPPED — `list_view/1` renders the empty
# state for a page that could not be read, and `Samen.UI.unread_state/1` itself is removed. This is
# the exact regression the whole primitive exists to prevent: an empty list communicates a claim
# about the DATA ("there is nothing here"), and a surface that renders a rescued query, an absent
# dependency table or a `{:error, _}` seam as an empty list is asserting something it never observed
# — the same lie ADR-014/024/026 forbid of an adapter (`{:ok, _}` for work it did not do). Removing
# the component takes its `:actions` slot with it, so a silence loses BOTH halves at once: the reader
# can no longer be told which outcome this is, nor what to do about it.
#
# Aimed at the `unread` contract ONLY: the `%Samen.Web.Page{}` field, the producers that set it, and
# every per-surface `unread` branch in the operator LiveViews are untouched. So the page still KNOWS
# it could not read; it simply has no way to say so, and silently claims the empty set instead —
# which is precisely the failure mode this patch makes the suite catch.
#
# No warning is introduced (a deleted function and a deleted clause leave nothing unused) and the
# replay runs `mix test`, so there is no warning to confine.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/unread_is_not_empty_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: list_view/1 renders the UNREAD state for a page that could not be read
# MUST_FAIL: unread_state/1 renders a state distinct from empty_state/1
# MUST_FAIL: unread_state/1 renders the NEXT STEP it is given
# MUST_FAIL: SABOTAGE TWIN — the SAME page renders the two states, so the probe discriminates
# MUST_FAIL: an unread page overrides even a caller-supplied :empty slot — a failure is not that surface's empty copy
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/ui/table.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/ui/table.ex
index 762dba0..721a18a 100644
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/ui/table.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/ui/table.ex
@@ -172,17 +172,6 @@ defmodule Samen.UI.Table do
           <div class="card list-loading" style="padding:14px 16px">
             <.skeleton rows={5} avatar />
           </div>
-        <% @page.items == [] and @page.unread != nil -> %>
-          <%!-- FAIL-HONEST: the read did not run (or did not succeed), so "no rows" is not a
-                claim this surface may make. The unread state is rendered INSTEAD of the empty
-                state, and BEFORE the `:empty` slot, so a caller cannot accidentally present a
-                failed read as its own tailored empty copy. --%>
-          <.unread_state
-            class="list-unread"
-            reason={@page.unread}
-            body={@empty_unread_body}
-            retry_event={@retry_event}
-          />
         <% @page.items == [] and @empty != [] -> %>
           {render_slot(@empty)}
         <% @page.items == [] -> %>
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/ui/feedback.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/ui/feedback.ex
index a1c2f86..9f10d80 100644
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/ui/feedback.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/ui/feedback.ex
@@ -58,125 +58,6 @@ defmodule Samen.UI.Feedback do
   # Unread state (fail-honest — the SIBLING of empty_state/1)
   # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
-  @doc """
-  The standard "this could not be read" state — the honest sibling of
-  `empty_state/1`, and NOT a variant of it.
-
-  ## Why it is a separate primitive
-
-  "Zero rows" and "we could not look" are different claims, and an empty list
-  communicates the first one whether or not it is true. Every surface that renders
-  a rescued query, an absent dependency table, or a `{:error, _}` seam as an empty
-  list is asserting something it did not observe — the exact lie ADR-014/024/026
-  forbid of an adapter (`{:ok, _}` for work it did not do). This component is how a
-  SURFACE keeps that same promise: it says what could not be read, why, and what
-  that means about the numbers beside it.
-
-  It is deliberately visually and textually distinct from `empty_state/1` — a
-  different glyph, a `data-read-state="unread"` marker, and the words "could not be
-  read" — so a screenshot of the two is not confusable, and a test can refute a
-  surface that swaps one for the other.
-
-  Purely presentational — copy in, markup out. It renders no field values, so it has
-  no masking surface.
-
-  ## `:actions` — a silence names its NEXT STEP, not only its reason
-
-  Naming what could not be read is half the honesty; the other half is what the reader can
-  DO about it. A silence with no next step strands the reader on the same page — and, worse,
-  invites them to read the neighbouring empty list as the answer, which is the collapse this
-  primitive exists to prevent. The `:actions` slot is where a surface supplies the step that
-  is actually available for THAT reason: a refused role → ask an owner to raise it; an
-  unmounted seam → the host's mount docs; a failed read → the operator runbook.
-
-  Two properties the CALLER owns (this component renders, it does not decide):
-
-    * **at most one step per reason** — a choice of remedies is a surface's design, and the
-      bounded silence vocabulary is one reason at a time;
-    * **a step is a link only to a destination that provably exists** — a route the host
-      declares (mount-label PRESENCE is the dead-link guard, the `Samen.UI.Nav` posture) or a
-      docs base it sets. Where the host declares neither, the destination is NAMED (a `code`
-      path on the span), never a href to a route nobody mounted and never a bare "see the
-      docs". Absent the slot, no affordance renders at all — a link to nowhere is the same
-      lie in a different costume.
-
-  Attrs:
-
-    * `title` — the headline (default "Could not be read.")
-    * `reason` — a bounded atom/term from the read layer (`:read_failed`,
-      `:not_mounted`, `:not_configured`, …), rendered as a monospace token so the
-      reader can name the failure in a bug report
-    * `body` — what this means (the default copy is the honest one; a caller with a
-      specific seam to name should override it)
-    * `retry_event` — OPTIONAL `phx-click` event name; when given, a Retry control
-      is rendered (a surface that can re-run its read should offer it)
-    * `:actions` — OPTIONAL slot, the next step(s) for this reason (see above)
-  """
-  attr :title, :string, default: "Could not be read."
-  attr :reason, :any, default: nil
-  attr :body, :string, default: nil
-  attr :retry_event, :string, default: nil
-  attr :class, :any, default: nil
-
-  slot :actions,
-    doc:
-      "the next step for THIS reason — the destination a caller has PROVEN exists on this host"
-
-  def unread_state(assigns) do
-    assigns =
-      assigns
-      |> assign(:class_attr, Enum.join(["card", "unread-state"] ++ List.wrap(assigns.class), " "))
-      |> assign(:reason_token, unread_reason_token(assigns.reason))
-      |> assign(
-        :body_text,
-        assigns.body ||
-          "This is not an empty result — nothing could be read here, so any count, total or " <>
-            "\"none yet\" statement on this surface would be a guess. Treat the absence as " <>
-            "unknown until the read succeeds."
-      )
-
-    ~H"""
-    <div
-      class={@class_attr}
-      data-read-state="unread"
-      style="padding:34px 24px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:8px;text-align:center"
-    >
-      <div class="unread-icon" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:26px;line-height:1">⚠</div>
-      <h3 class="unread-title" style="margin:0;font-size:15px;font-weight:600">{@title}</h3>
-      <p :if={@reason_token} class="unread-reason" style="margin:0;color:var(--muted);font-size:13px">
-        reason: <span class="mono" data-unread-reason={@reason_token}>{@reason_token}</span>
-      </p>
-      <p class="unread-body" style="margin:0;color:var(--muted);font-size:13px;max-width:52ch">{@body_text}</p>
-      <div
-        :if={@actions != []}
-        class="unread-actions"
-        style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin-top:8px"
-      >
-        {render_slot(@actions)}
-      </div>
-      <button
-        :if={@retry_event}
-        type="button"
-        class="btn-retry"
-        phx-click={@retry_event}
-        style="margin-top:8px;padding:7px 14px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid var(--line2);background:var(--card);font-size:13px;cursor:pointer"
-      >
-        Retry
-      </button>
-    </div>
-    """
-  end
-
-  # The bounded token a reader can quote: an atom/string as-is, a `{tag, _detail}` tuple
-  # by its tag (the detail is a raw error term and never belongs in the DOM), and anything
-  # else by its inspect form. `nil` renders no reason line at all.
-  @doc false
-  def unread_reason_token(nil), do: nil
-  def unread_reason_token(reason) when is_atom(reason), do: to_string(reason)
-  def unread_reason_token(reason) when is_binary(reason), do: reason
-  def unread_reason_token({tag, _detail}) when is_atom(tag), do: to_string(tag)
-  def unread_reason_token(reason), do: inspect(reason)
-
   # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   # Skeleton (WS-E E6.2, ADR-030 — the loading-placeholder primitive)
   # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
